A||||14||Homicidal||Different Sub Boxes: Pros and Cons||||1||
Z||000000||Homicidal||08-05-2000||03:39 AM||||I am not a huge guy, and I like driving a bit close to the steering column, so I made a custom box for my Polk Audio db 10".  My LORD this thing ROCKS.  I listen to ALL music, and since it's a totally sealed box, it has all the power to push my Sevendust and Slipknot to my 2-Pac and Bone Thugs.  <P>I really prefer this to any other suggestion on the board.  <P><B>The footwell has too many flaws:</B><P>a)Can be kicked unless you got a covering.<P>b)Limits the passenger space (not a problem if you drive alone though).<P>c)I have a 12 cd changer behind the passenger seat.<P>d)Easily seen, easily stolen.<P>e)Just doesn't look GOOD.<P><B>The front box:</B><P>a)Must be bandbass to be heard WELL.<P>b)70% goes to the outside, cabin only gets a bit.<P>c)Sux on freeway!<P>d)Hard to build an angeled box.<P>e)Wires are harder to run.<P>The problem with <B>my setup:</B><P>a)Limits driving space (not for me though).<P>That's all I can think of for my setup.  It's actually NOT easily seen, people don't see it unless they are driving with me or I point it out.  It can be ported to give more UMPF also.  It hits MEGA hard inside the car, and easily heard outside the car! It handled all music also.  And the passenger remains free to move around.  Oh yah, it also acts as a shelf to place my misc crap like cases and shirts and stuff!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>If anybody wants a pic of my setup and/or the box, lemme know!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Homicidal||08-05-2000||03:47 AM||||I just realized I only listed cons for the other suggestions.  my bad!  Anybody is more than welcome to put those in for me!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||08-05-2000||04:23 AM||||Well, you can always but the box behind the passenger seat...<P>Could you send me the dimensions of your box?  Pics would be cool too!<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 148,000 miles and counting!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||08-05-2000||12:36 PM||||I'm a little confused, are you lookng for feedback, or are you just saying that your idea is the best? If it works for you, more power to you. If you are seriously considering an alternative to a big pressboard shoebox stuffed behind your seat, then I would be happy to respond to some of your comments.   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Homicidal:<BR><B>The footwell has too many flaws<P>a)Can be kicked unless you got a covering.<BR></B>Simple answer. Waffle grill cost between $4-8 depending on how much you shop around. It can even be dressed up by attaching headliner-type fabric with spray glue and painting the clips and rubber edge with interior paint to match the color of your interior.<B><P>b)Limits the passenger space (not a problem if you drive alone though).<BR></B>Really not a problem if you don't. The enclosure I made is about 8" deep at it's deepest point. It only takes up the same amount of space that the pedals use on the drivers side. I'm 6'6" tall and have no problem sitting comfortably on the passenger side. Unless your girl is in the WNBA, you should be cool.<B><P>c)I have a 12 cd changer behind the passenger seat.<BR></B>Well, move it! I'm positive it has smaller dimensions then your box. It can just as easily go behind your seat. With 12 CD's, you really don't need to be changing out the cartridge whle you are driving, and it's unsafe to be doing that if its behind the passenger<B><P>d)Easily seen, easily stolen.<BR></B>Anything can be stolen if the thief wants it bad enough. If you are inclined, I'm sure you could devise a method of permanently mounting a footwell sub. I don't worry too uch because my state laws allow for dark tint on the side windows, you cannot see my sub from outside the car, especially at night. Also an alarm is always a good investment.<B><BR> <BR>e)Just doesn't look GOOD.<BR></B>Beg to differ on that count.  I have had many compliments on the appearance of my sub enclosure. I used factory carpet salvaged from the Pick and Pull (free!) to cover the front of the box. It really does look like it belongs there.  I agree that prefabricated "black boxes" laid on the floor in the passenger side are a bit of an eyesore, I think my box looks (.)(.)'s!<P><B>The front box:</B><P><B>a)Must be bandpass to be heard WELL.<BR></B>Also should be ported to the cabin to work effectively. Get out your Sawzall!<P><B>b)70% goes to the outside, cabin only gets a bit.<BR></B>Thereby advertising to all the local crackheads that there is something tradeable for a $5 rock i your car. <P><B>c)Sux on freeway!<BR></B>Probably. <P><B>d)Hard to build an angeled box.<BR></B> But you can buy pre-fabbed box from <A HREF="http://www.subbox.com" TARGET=_blank>www.subbox.com</A> <BR><B>e)Wires are harder to run.<BR></B>but you already cut a bigass hole in your floorboard to run the port!<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Homi, please don't take this as flaming you. I'm not trying to change your mind. But others may be thinking about going with the footwell plan (which was the <B>only</B> viable option for me) and I'd hate for them to be discouraged. I still need to scan my pics to put them up, but I think you will be impressed with the results.<P><BR>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://gifs123.tripod.com/page15/renstimpy2.gif">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 08-05-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000004||Homicidal||08-05-2000||01:08 PM||||Hey, you had every right to counter my post!  In fact, you pointed out some very good points.<P>It seesm we both kind of agree that the front box enclosure is the WORST of them all.<P>Nah, mine isn't the best.  It's the best for me, and I was wondering if anybody would prove me that the footwell or other might work better.||||reg||12
Z||000005||stimpy||08-05-2000||03:44 PM||||I think it ould be the best bet for <B>most</B> people. Pics later today I hope.||||reg||1
Z||000006||86SE||08-05-2000||04:07 PM||||Im thinkin about building a box for the front compartment that will hold 2 10's then port it throught the air condition system some how.....<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||10
Z||000007||Formula 18||08-05-2000||11:24 PM||||Far be it from me to to disagree with the brilliant GM engineers... so I stuck mine 10" inch MTX sub in a custom box that fits under the passager dash. The only downfall is that i had to move a few things and it took about 4 days to get it it fit (read HIT) just right. <BR>Brian ||||reg||1
Z||000008||DaRkLoRD||08-06-2000||12:21 AM||||Formula 18, could you post some pics of your install? I'd like to do a similar setup, and would love to hear how you did this.. what had to be modified, etc..<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A> <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000009||Black88GT||08-06-2000||12:31 AM||||The footwell is the best spot.  I had a custom fiberglass box built for a 10", when it sits back in the footwell, you can barely even see it from the pass. seat much less outside.  Who would not cover it?  I think "somebody could kick it" is hardly a decent argument.  I am assuming you put yours behind the drivers seat? Thats dumb because what if someone tall wants to drive yur car?  Doesn't it drive you nuts with yur back vibrating the entire way?  If anything, put it behind the pass. seat and change the location of the changer.<P><BR>jeff||||reg||1
Z||000010||Homicidal||08-06-2000||12:32 AM||||A) NOBODY drives mu car except ME!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>B) No, it doesn't vibrate my back since it's pointed towards the firewall and the wood is thick enough to deter it away from the seat.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Formula||08-06-2000||09:47 AM||||not to toot anybodys horn, but have any of actually heard a sub in the front?<P>How about a powerful sub and a powerful amp, the theft stuff really doesnt apply to me here way out in the country.  A lot of people say that my sub sounds good and these are people that build 150-160db competition stereos for cars.  Sure, I can probably rip up in the drive by spl class because I have a 10" and a small amp compared to most of them there.  I dont know what you mean by you cant hear it on the highway? I can drive fine on the highway and hear it.  The main reason I went with the front trunk is because I need the passenger foot room and I didnt want to cut a hole in my firewall.  And believe it or not the wires are probably easier to run to the front of the car then to go back behind the dash to get it into the footwell.  I think that its up to what the person wants and/or has money to pay for.  AND I think you should hear mine before you go saying its the worse type of box out there.......You might change your mind.<P>  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||spike||08-06-2000||10:16 AM||||I am a big bass fan and loud, hard hitting music is for me. When I had my previous Fiero GT I had built a box that covered the entire rear window. The box itself was fitted piece buy piece. I had made a plexi window on the front plate and rear of the box so I could see behind my. When I made the face plate I made sure that it followed the contours of the roof and inner panels. this box fit so tight that I did not have to bolt it it. I was planning on building one for my new ride but I am debating on going topless so I might have to think of something else. The box was not quite the recommended volume for my 2 10 inch subs but the sound was great. It costed me about 80.00 cdn. to build. The whole trick to making this box look real good is the face plate. If you do it right there is no space between it and the inside car pannels. It actually looks factory. I covered it (the face plate only) with matching gray vynle. I had made notches in the face plate to fit around the center console and the sunroof latch. I wish I had pictures to show you people but soory I don't. This is where I would put my subs if it were up to me. Trust me people it really looks great. For my amp I removed the door on the center console and slid it in. My amp just happened to be the perfect size. The only problen with this setup is that everything especialy the amp is visable. I good alarm system is needed. To cover my amp up I made a vynle flap which I would wrap aroud the exposed portion and attached it with velcro. If you like big bass build this box and you won't be sorry.<P>Tks, Mike.<P>PS: Trust me it looks perfect. ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Philphine||08-06-2000||10:23 AM||||i have an 8 in the passenger foot well. the two biggest sound competition system fieros i've seen had them in the front trunk (pro built mega system) and behind the seats (fierosound, put your 2 cents in here). i went with an 8 because i thought a 10 would take up too much room, but now i'm adding to the system (8's in the doors) but a future system in another fiero may get a 10 since others seem to be satisfied with the foot room they have left.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe<P>any body remember for a while there was someone advertising plans to put 4 12's in a fiero. any body buy them or know what they were?<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 08-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||MooCow||08-07-2000||12:04 AM||||Soon I will be taking out the first fire wall and will see how much actual room there is and see if I can get 4 10"s or 2 12"s.  Just have to come up with a little more money and pick out my subs I wish to use.  The amps will be mounted in the front.  The subs will be used with vynal for the finished look.  I will let you know how it turns out when I get to working on it.<P>Right now I have two rockford 8" behind the seats with the amp.  It hits really hard and I only lost 2 clicks but then again im only 5'5" so I am happy with is.<BR>  <BR>                              Thanks Ken||||reg||10
